        office, the ``primary`` argument only has an effect if the value of
        ``length`` is ``11``. If ``primary`` is ``True`` and ``length`` is ``11``,
        the 11-digit SWIFT codes generated will always end in ``'XXX'`` to denote
        that they belong to primary branches/offices.

        For extra authenticity, localized providers may opt to include SWIFT bank
        codes, location codes, and branch codes used in their respective locales. If
        ``use_dataset`` is ``True``, this method will generate SWIFT codes based on
        those locale-specific codes if included. If those codes were not included,
        then it will behave as if ``use_dataset`` were ``False``, and in that mode,
        all those codes will just be randomly generated as per the specification.

